{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1098597-bit-of-help-with-a-scion-that-went-off-the-rails","id":1098597,"title":"Bit of help with a scion that went off the rails","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-30T16:00:19-07:00","id":1098597,"title":"Bit of help with a scion that went off the rails","content":"So, I'm starting a game to hold my group over until 2nd. The initial set-up is that they all converge on a certain location at the same, the place the think someon the out hits out on them is hiding.<br /> <br /> The mastermind her is a scion, who believes divine power is finite and wants to tear down all but his parent pantheon so they can singlhandly crush the titan. Now he came this idea on his own but I can't figure out who a good Dive parent for him is.<br /> <br /> Out group so far is a scion of Twzcatlipoca inspired by Dexter Morgan, a scion of Ptah with a background in pro gaming, and a scion of Henza who's served time in a Chinese Juvie center. Their all either mental or scocial based so I want an idea that can play off that as they delve deeper. I don't want to go with the standard &quot;Loki's the bad guy&quot; reasoning so I'm trying to look at the Greeks or Japanize since they seem to have the worst combinations or arrogant and Xenophobic.<br /> <br /> So does anyone know a god that is likely to spawn a divine Hannibal Lecter but isn't from the player pantheons I mentioned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T16:59:33-07:00","id":1098615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1098597-bit-of-help-with-a-scion-that-went-off-the-rails#post1098597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm starting a game to hold my group over until 2nd. The initial set-up is that they all converge on a certain location at the same, the place the think someon the out hits out on them is hiding.<br /> <br /> The mastermind her is a scion, who believes divine power is finite and wants to tear down all but his parent pantheon so they can singlhandly crush the titan. Now he came this idea on his own but I can't figure out who a good Dive parent for him is.<br /> <br /> Out group so far is a scion of Twzcatlipoca inspired by Dexter Morgan, a scion of Ptah with a background in pro gaming, and a scion of Henza who's served time in a Chinese Juvie center. Their all either mental or scocial based so I want an idea that can play off that as they delve deeper. I don't want to go with the standard &quot;Loki's the bad guy&quot; reasoning so I'm trying to look at the Greeks or Japanize since they seem to have the worst combinations or arrogant and Xenophobic.<br /> <br /> So does anyone know a god that is likely to spawn a divine Hannibal Lecter but isn't from the player pantheons I mentioned?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only Divine Parent that leaps to mind between the Theoi and the Kami is Izanami if you are looking for someone who is 'close' to their Divine Parent in concept. In my revision of the Kami, I made Izanami a Titan since she is a) horribly antagonistic to Gods and Mortals b) got put in a box, and c) old and powerful, but in RAW she is listed as one of the potential Divine Parents. If you are playing from RAW, she is not a bad option for Divine Parent for this Scion.<br /> <br /> Izanami and Izanagi are caught in this back and forth of Izanami killing off mortals, and Izanagi causing more mortals to be born. One thousand mortals die per day, and one thousand five hundred born. Obviously these numbers probably sounded more impressive back when the story was in it's prime. She doesn't have the greatest thoughts and feelings towards her own Pantheon either, so that could work as well.<br /> <br /> If you want to subvert expectations, you could go with a Divine Parent who has no connection to mass deicide. Everyone always suspects the Scion of Loki, but the Scion of Inari is <i>totally</i> out of left field.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T20:36:41-07:00","id":1098643,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the advice, I'm not neccacarily looking for someone identical to their divne parent, but rather one that could both logically trick themselves into belieaveing cull other dcions will help in the long run, and clever enough to give them a bit of a run around, I'm looking for a good well intentioned extremist really/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T21:11:58-07:00","id":1098651,"title":"","content":"Ah, okay! Well, I can give some more suggestions in that case.<ul><li><b>Scion of Nike</b>: Minor Goddess, since it is for an NPC you don't need to come up with a statline of favored things for her. Play off the idea of Victory at Any Cost, and instead of being smart they could instead be preternaturally lucky. They, as a child of Success incarnate, are just going wild with their capacity to pull things off they have no right to. This will, in the end, be Fated to come crashing down upon their heads as the Theoi do not regard uppity Scions highly, and the Fates of such Grecian Heroes tend to be tragic. They would likely fail in some ironic way in the end, being too lucky, having the Theoi reject their preposterous idea when they try to announce to the Pantheon their good works, such things.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Scion of Athena</b>: A Philosopher who has come to the following conclusions. Based on the Age of Saturn theory, the further from the origin of the world one is, the weaker they are. So, the Primordials are stronger than the Titans who are stronger than the Gods who are stronger than Mortals. Mortals from the Age of Gold are stronger than Silver, than Heroic, than Iron. They reason that, in fact, it has nothing to do with the distance from the cosmic origins, but actually population of a generation. There are <i>very</i> few Primordials, there are more Titans, and even more Gods. They reason that the reason each generation of creation is less and less powerful is because of a set pool of power per generation, and thus if they were to try to cull other Scions, they could increase their own power, etc. They could be very smart, they could explain their theory very convincingly, but be utterly wrong. Put up against someone with higher Epic Intelligence, they could be fought on a philosophical ground.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T21:25:04-07:00","id":1098654,"title":"","content":"What about a scion of Odin, Zeus or similar? Given that the Fates/Norns never said any other pantheons would be present for the Last Days, they could easily be led to conclude that the other gods needed to be removed and their powers added to the home team. It could be twisted to look like part of their duty to their pantheon to ensure that the other gods' gifts, birthrights and very lives were sacrificed in the name of the &quot;greater&quot; good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1098597-bit-of-help-with-a-scion-that-went-off-the-rails?p=1098651#post1098651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li><b>Scion of Athena</b>: A Philosopher who has come to the following conclusions. Based on the Age of Saturn theory, the further from the origin of the world one is, the weaker they are. So, the Primordials are stronger than the Titans who are stronger than the Gods who are stronger than Mortals. Mortals from the Age of Gold are stronger than Silver, than Heroic, than Iron. They reason that, in fact, it has nothing to do with the distance from the cosmic origins, but actually population of a generation. There are <i>very</i> few Primordials, there are more Titans, and even more Gods. They reason that the reason each generation of creation is less and less powerful is because of a set pool of power per generation, and thus if they were to try to cull other Scions, they could increase their own power, etc. They could be very smart, they could explain their theory very convincingly, but be utterly wrong. Put up against someone with higher Epic Intelligence, they could be fought on a philosophical ground.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>You could also steal a leaf from Vampire's book here and have them believe that a transfusion of ichor is useful for &quot;supercharging&quot; their own pantheon's powers. And since ichor can only be found in divine entities...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13499-not-quite-yoda","name":"Not Quite Yoda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T03:16:21-07:00","id":1098720,"title":"","content":"Ok, I really like all those ideas. I think I might use the scion of Athena as the &quot;Big bad&quot; and ones of Nike and Zeus, and maybe throw in a dupe from Ares as catspaws. And obvious mix in some good scions from the family just to keep it from being &quot;Or look, Greeks are evil&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thanks, this helps me give a lot more structure to the plot I had in mind. And the Scion of Nike sort of reveling in her good luck highlights the temptation of power theme I wanted the campaign to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}